 "_note": "Derived independently of engine/scoring.js from the documented rules. Item value = reverse ? 4 - response : response. Facet = sum of its 4 items (0-16). Every scale above facet level = the signed sum of its `members` (aspect and domain sums are unsigned; Stability = -Neuroticism + Agreeableness + Conscientiousness). Bands are NORM-REFERENCED: percentile = Phi((score - mean) / sd) against the default norm group (u21-all), with Phi computed here by Simpson-rule integration rather than the rational approximation used in scoring.js. Note that all-midpoint no longer lands mid-range everywhere: answering \"neither accurate nor inaccurate\" to all 120 items is itself an unusual profile relative to the norms, which is exactly what criterion-referenced thirds were hiding.",
